    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44143" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὔιος </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὔἱος</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>EM</u>
			391.15
		</span></i>, cf. Lat. <u>Euhius</u>), ὁ,
		name of Bacchus, from the cry <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐαἵ,
		εὐοἱ</span>, in lyr. passages, <i><span class="en">
			S.
			<u>OT</u>
			211
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Ba.</u>
			157
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Ecphantid.
			3
		</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὔιος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάκχος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				566
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				579
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔιος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, as Adj., <u>Bacchic</u>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ</span>”
